# station.conf — where your receiver physically is, plus local tuning.
#
#     cp station.conf.example station.conf
#     $EDITOR station.conf
#     ./install.sh
#
# This file is gitignored. Your coordinates are personal data: combined with
# the timestamps in captures/, they pin down your home. Ship the example, never
# the real one.
#
# The ':' + ':=' form means an environment variable wins over the file, so
# `LAT=40.5 ./install.sh` still works for a one-off.

# ---- Receiver position -------------------------------------------------------
# Decimal degrees. South and West are negative.
# Enables map centering and range rings.
#
# For MLAT this is NOT good enough: multilateration solves position from
# nanosecond time-of-arrival differences, so a receiver location that is off by
# even ~50 m poisons the solution for everyone in your cluster. If you ever feed
# MLAT, replace this with your actual antenna position from a phone GPS or from
# Google Maps satellite view, to 5 decimal places.

# : "${LAT:=00.00000}"
# : "${LON:=000.00000}"

# Antenna height is deliberately absent: readsb has no altitude flag (verified
# against `readsb --help`). Height is an mlat-client parameter, supplied there.

# ---- Tuning ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Tuner gain. 'auto' is right for most setups. A specific dB value can beat it
# when a strong local transmitter is desensitising the front end.
# : "${GAIN:=auto}"

# CPU relief for weak boards. readsb's own help: "lower threshold -> more CPU
# usage (default: 58, pi zero / pi 1: 75, hot CPU 42)".
# : "${PREAMBLE:=75}"

# Feeder flush interval in seconds. 3600 = hourly.
# : "${INTERVAL:=3600}"
